WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.834
-Looking good. Looking sharp.
-Good to be back!

00:00:02.834 --> 00:00:05.367
-Yes, you're actually back.
-In person.

00:00:05.367 --> 00:00:06.868
-The last time we talked,
you guys were --

00:00:06.868 --> 00:00:08.367
Actually, you weren't even
together.

00:00:08.367 --> 00:00:10.701
You were -- We're all Zooming.
-That's right.

00:00:10.701 --> 00:00:14.701
-And that was the first time you
guys had been apart in over --

00:00:14.701 --> 00:00:16.133
-Many, many years.
-Oh, yeah.

00:00:16.133 --> 00:00:18.767
-Is it 20 years? Because you've
been friends forever.

00:00:18.767 --> 00:00:20.901
-Yeah.
The pandemic took us apart

00:00:20.901 --> 00:00:22.901
for a little bit over a month.
-Yeah.

00:00:22.901 --> 00:00:25.701
-That's when we were getting
together with you over the Zoom.

00:00:25.701 --> 00:00:27.734
It was tough.
It was tough on our friendship.

00:00:27.734 --> 00:00:29.501
-I was talking to myself a lot.

00:00:29.501 --> 00:00:31.701
But I learned a lot about myself
apart from Link.

00:00:31.701 --> 00:00:33.300
-But then when you got
back together,

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:34.834
you wanted to do it in
the safest way possible.

00:00:34.834 --> 00:00:36.734
-You got to maintain
that social distance.

00:00:36.734 --> 00:00:38.567
Six feet.
-Yeah, you brought a photo.

00:00:38.567 --> 00:00:40.868
And just for us, I really
appreciate this exclusive photo.

00:00:40.868 --> 00:00:41.868
This is you...
-Oh, yeah.

00:00:41.868 --> 00:00:43.300
-...meeting for the first time.

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:45.501
There you go. Maintain that --
[ Laughter ]

00:00:45.501 --> 00:00:47.634
You can still feel the love.
[ Applause ]

00:00:47.634 --> 00:00:48.801
-Yes.

00:00:48.801 --> 00:00:50.267
-Those are my arms though.

00:00:50.267 --> 00:00:52.400
Rhett had to get an extension.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:53.667
-Those are your actual arms.
Yeah.

00:00:53.667 --> 00:00:56.534
-I get those long arms.

00:00:56.534 --> 00:00:59.033
-You just celebrated 10 years
of the show, by the way.

00:00:59.033 --> 00:01:00.234
Congratulations.
-Crazy.

00:01:00.234 --> 00:01:01.367
-That's amazing.
-A decade.

00:01:01.367 --> 00:01:05.434
-10 years, over 2,000 episodes.

00:01:05.434 --> 00:01:08.067
-You have nearly 8 billion
views.

00:01:08.067 --> 00:01:10.968
Do you know that? Were those
the dreams when you first

00:01:10.968 --> 00:01:12.133
started the show 10 years ago?

00:01:12.133 --> 00:01:14.133
Like, "Wow, we're gonna hit
8 billion views"?

00:01:14.133 --> 00:01:16.234
-Well, we just thought,
"You know what?

00:01:16.234 --> 00:01:18.701
If we can enjoy hanging out with
each other for all this time,

00:01:18.701 --> 00:01:21.834
let's just start putting that on
the Internet and see if people

00:01:21.834 --> 00:01:23.100
can latch on to it."

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:25.100
In the first episode,
we were talking about,

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:27.100
"Hey, this is going to be
something big.

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:29.367
Make this a part of
your daily routine."

00:01:29.367 --> 00:01:31.467
And I mean, I think we were just
saying that to pump ourselves.

00:01:31.467 --> 00:01:34.334
-Yeah, we were hyping ourselves.
-But it turns out we were, like,

00:01:34.334 --> 00:01:37.300
speaking it into existence.
I did not know I had this power.

00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:39.067
-Yeah, I mean, because it's been
cool to see

00:01:39.067 --> 00:01:40.567
the mythical beasts out there.

00:01:40.567 --> 00:01:42.767
They're so supportive of
what we're doing,

00:01:42.767 --> 00:01:44.634
and they've grown up over
these past 10 years.

00:01:44.634 --> 00:01:47.200
We've had people grow up,
get married.

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:48.868
We've had people get divorced,

00:01:48.868 --> 00:01:51.434
which those can be really
interesting because

00:01:51.434 --> 00:01:53.968
if you have family that is
watching the show

00:01:53.968 --> 00:01:55.133
and they get divorced,
they start two new families.

00:01:55.133 --> 00:01:56.534
-Twice as many views.

00:01:56.534 --> 00:01:57.968
-That's a great way
to double your fan base.

00:01:57.968 --> 00:02:00.100
-Oh, so you double the --
That's how you get to 8 billion.

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:01.367
That's genius.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:02:01.367 --> 00:02:02.734
-Brilliantly said.
-Right.

00:02:02.734 --> 00:02:03.868
-Yeah.
-Wow.

00:02:03.868 --> 00:02:06.434
[ Applause ]

00:02:06.434 --> 00:02:09.534
You're almost encouraging all of
your fans to get divorced.

00:02:09.534 --> 00:02:10.767
You want to hit 16 billion
views.

00:02:10.767 --> 00:02:12.801
-But they're starting good,
new families. See?

00:02:12.801 --> 00:02:14.634
-Of course.
-I'm a product of divorce.

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:15.801
Look at me.
-Look at you.

00:02:15.801 --> 00:02:17.534
Look at how good he turned out.
Fantastic.

00:02:17.534 --> 00:02:20.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:20.534 --> 00:02:21.968
Here's a pic.

00:02:21.968 --> 00:02:24.267
Here's a pic from your very
first "Good Mythical Morning."

00:02:24.267 --> 00:02:27.133
-Haven't changed a bit.
-Haven't changed a bit at all.

00:02:27.133 --> 00:02:31.100
Did you always sit on
the same sides, Rhett &amp; Link?

00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:34.901
-Yeah. We have always sat as
Rhett &amp; Link in order to

00:02:34.901 --> 00:02:38.667
not be confused as
Link &amp; Rhett.

00:02:38.667 --> 00:02:41.234
-That's the last thing I want,
is to be confused as him.

00:02:41.234 --> 00:02:43.968
-That's the last thing you want.
-But, see, here's the thing.

00:02:43.968 --> 00:02:47.434
The way that works out here is
that, you know,

00:02:47.434 --> 00:02:48.801
this is the eighth time
we've been here.

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:50.167
Seventh time we've been here
in person.

00:02:50.167 --> 00:02:51.434
-Yeah, of course.

00:02:51.434 --> 00:02:53.734
-Every single time,
he gets to sit close to you.

00:02:53.734 --> 00:02:55.133
-Because you're Rhett
and you're Link?

00:02:55.133 --> 00:02:56.467
-Yeah.
-That's the way it works.

00:02:56.467 --> 00:02:58.567
-And I'd like to know
what it feels like.

00:02:58.567 --> 00:02:59.934
[ Laughter ]

00:02:59.934 --> 00:03:01.734
-To sit here?
-Yeah.

00:03:01.734 --> 00:03:06.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:06.968 --> 00:03:08.334
-Will you let me?

00:03:08.334 --> 00:03:09.734
-No.

00:03:09.734 --> 00:03:13.200
No. No. I like how --
I like the arrangement.

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:14.834
-I don't think I have to
ask for permission.

00:03:14.834 --> 00:03:17.067
[ Laughter ]
-Hey.

00:03:17.067 --> 00:03:19.234
[ Cheers and applause ]
This feels pretty good.

00:03:19.234 --> 00:03:21.000
-Did I just disappear entirely?

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:23.534
-Yes, no one can see you at all,
by the way.

00:03:23.534 --> 00:03:26.400
They can't see you.
He is there somewhere.

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:27.667
-Wow.
-How's it feel?

00:03:27.667 --> 00:03:28.701
-You're a good-looking guy.

00:03:28.701 --> 00:03:31.067
-Thank you. You too.
-Hey.

00:03:31.067 --> 00:03:32.567
-It's great to see you, bud.
You're a stud.

00:03:32.567 --> 00:03:35.300
-You're going to mess up
the cords in my corduroy.

00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:36.801
Get off.
-Alright, alright.

00:03:36.801 --> 00:03:38.968
That's all I need.
-"What you want for Christmas?"

00:03:38.968 --> 00:03:41.167
-I want to talk about --
You guys are hosting a new show

00:03:41.167 --> 00:03:42.834
on the Food Network.
-Yeah.

00:03:42.834 --> 00:03:44.367
-I love Food Network.
-After tasting food for like

00:03:44.367 --> 00:03:46.400
10 years on
"Good Mythical Morning,"

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:49.167
then Food Network gives you
a show to taste more food.

00:03:49.167 --> 00:03:52.467
But we get to leave our studio
and go out on --

00:03:52.467 --> 00:03:54.300
I'll call them "adventures."

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:56.701
Behind the scenes of some of
your favorite restaurants.

00:03:56.701 --> 00:03:58.400
-Because it's called
"Inside Eats."

00:03:58.400 --> 00:03:59.601
-That's right.
-"With Rhett &amp; Link."

00:03:59.601 --> 00:04:01.033
So you get on the inside.

00:04:01.033 --> 00:04:03.200
-Yeah, we ask questions like,

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:06.567
"Why is The Cheesecake Factory
menu so big?"

00:04:06.567 --> 00:04:07.934
[ Laughter ]

00:04:07.934 --> 00:04:08.934
-Yeah, that's a great question.
-"What happened there?

00:04:08.934 --> 00:04:10.234
Why is it spiral-bound?"

00:04:10.234 --> 00:04:11.300
-"And how do they do that?

00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:13.701
How do they pull off
so many items?"

00:04:13.701 --> 00:04:15.701
-Yeah.
-You know?

00:04:15.701 --> 00:04:18.667
-Like, I know you recently did
one with Chipotle.

00:04:18.667 --> 00:04:20.000
-Oh, yes.
-Yes.

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:22.767
Well, see, we think that what
you order at Chipotle

00:04:22.767 --> 00:04:24.300
says something about
your personality.

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:26.801
We believe in this so strongly
that we think that we can

00:04:26.801 --> 00:04:30.067
actually get to know somebody,
ask them a few questions

00:04:30.067 --> 00:04:32.801
and then predict what
their Chipotle order is.

00:04:32.801 --> 00:04:35.167
-We can do it for you right now.

00:04:35.167 --> 00:04:37.100
-You can -- You can tell what --

00:04:37.100 --> 00:04:39.601
-We can predict
your Chipotle order.

00:04:39.601 --> 00:04:41.701
Okay, so what is your sign?

00:04:41.701 --> 00:04:43.033
-Alright, here we go.
What's going on?

00:04:43.033 --> 00:04:44.267
-Focus, Jimmy. What's your sign?

00:04:44.267 --> 00:04:45.567
-Alright, do I look straight?

00:04:45.567 --> 00:04:47.434
-Look at me.
-Sorry, alright.

00:04:47.434 --> 00:04:50.501
-Hold up your left hand
and your right hand.

00:04:50.501 --> 00:04:52.067
What's your sign?
-Virgo.

00:04:52.067 --> 00:04:54.133
-What's your favorite color?

00:04:54.133 --> 00:04:55.267
-Right now, red.

00:04:55.267 --> 00:04:58.234
-Okay, and then clasp
your hands.

00:04:58.234 --> 00:04:59.868
-What's the worst thing
you've ever done?

00:04:59.868 --> 00:05:02.167
[ Laughter ]

00:05:02.167 --> 00:05:05.100
-I tried to pull off
cargo shorts once.

00:05:05.100 --> 00:05:06.934
[ Laughter ]

00:05:06.934 --> 00:05:08.100
I shouldn't have done that.
-Alright.

00:05:08.100 --> 00:05:09.501
Those are burrito-grabbing
hands.

00:05:09.501 --> 00:05:10.634
I think he's a burrito man.
-Hold on.

00:05:10.634 --> 00:05:13.234
Let me test. Grab that forearm.

00:05:13.234 --> 00:05:14.801
Oh, you're a burrito man.

00:05:14.801 --> 00:05:16.200
-Burrito guy.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:18.400
-Okay.
-This is ridiculous.

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:21.000
-Look at me deeply in the eyes.
-Yes, I always do.

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:23.234
-Black beans.

00:05:23.234 --> 00:05:25.100
-White rice.

00:05:25.100 --> 00:05:26.901
-Yes, that's a burrito.
Isn't it?

00:05:26.901 --> 00:05:28.100
[ Laughter ]

00:05:28.100 --> 00:05:29.868
-Protein.
-Give me an "ah."

00:05:29.868 --> 00:05:31.033
-Ah.

00:05:31.033 --> 00:05:32.267
-He's a chicken man.

00:05:32.267 --> 00:05:33.567
-Chicken man.

00:05:33.567 --> 00:05:36.100
Alright, and your left ear,
I'm sorry to say this,

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:39.000
is a little lower
than your right ear.

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:40.300
[ Laughter ]

00:05:40.300 --> 00:05:42.000
-So what does that tell you?

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:44.634
-You hate sour cream.

00:05:44.634 --> 00:05:47.868
You can't stand sour cream.

00:05:47.868 --> 00:05:49.701
-That is true.
I do not like sour cream.

00:05:49.701 --> 00:05:50.968
-Right, right.
-Hey, we're professionals.

00:05:50.968 --> 00:05:52.868
-It's the ear thing. Yeah.

00:05:52.868 --> 00:05:56.000
And then you like it spicy.
-A little spice.

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:58.267
-Okay. This is actually correct.

00:05:58.267 --> 00:05:59.734
This is bizarre.
-Yeah, right.

00:05:59.734 --> 00:06:00.801
-Okay.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:06:00.801 --> 00:06:02.267
-We do this for a living, Jimmy.

00:06:02.267 --> 00:06:04.701
-Right, so what you're saying is
my order is,

00:06:04.701 --> 00:06:07.734
is a spicy chicken burrito
with --

00:06:07.734 --> 00:06:10.901
-White rice, black beans.
-No sour cream.

00:06:10.901 --> 00:06:13.067
-That is absolutely correct,
by the way.

00:06:13.067 --> 00:06:15.734
[ Cheers and applause ]
That is 100% correct.

00:06:20.300 --> 00:06:22.167
-We didn't get you one though.
I'm sorry.

00:06:22.167 --> 00:06:23.567
-No, you didn't get me one.

00:06:23.567 --> 00:06:26.501
Did you ask around or something?
-Of course we didn't ask

00:06:26.501 --> 00:06:27.834
your producers ahead of time

00:06:27.834 --> 00:06:29.667
what you normally order
from Chipotle.

00:06:29.667 --> 00:06:30.734
[ Laughter ]

00:06:30.734 --> 00:06:32.400
-I was wondering.
I go, "Oh, my gosh.

00:06:32.400 --> 00:06:35.300
Wait a second, you're actually
on -- totally on point."

00:06:35.300 --> 00:06:37.400
Someone told you. Perfect.
Alright. Good.

00:06:37.400 --> 00:06:39.968
[ Laughter ]
I want to show a clip.

00:06:39.968 --> 00:06:41.501
What are we going to see here
for your show?

00:06:41.501 --> 00:06:43.434
-Well, we went to Beyond Meat.

00:06:43.434 --> 00:06:44.467
-Oh!
[ Audience oohs ]

00:06:44.467 --> 00:06:45.901
-You're intrigued now.

00:06:45.901 --> 00:06:47.701
-If you've ever seen meat,
it's on the other side of that.

00:06:47.701 --> 00:06:50.567
-It's "beyond," yeah. It's like,
"Bed, Bath, and Beyond Meat."

00:06:50.567 --> 00:06:52.200
-Right, exactly.

00:06:52.200 --> 00:06:53.968
-We kind of went behind the
scenes, got the whole process,

00:06:53.968 --> 00:06:56.667
How they make
this plant-based meat.

00:06:56.667 --> 00:06:58.334
And we had a little taste test.
-Oh!

00:06:58.334 --> 00:07:00.601
-A blind taste test.
-Oh, here's a look.

00:07:00.601 --> 00:07:03.000
"Inside Eats with Rhett &amp; Link."
Take a look.

00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:07.634
-How much do you like or dislike
the appearance of your sample?

00:07:07.634 --> 00:07:10.300
-I like it very much.

00:07:10.300 --> 00:07:12.868
-And you don't say your answers
out loud.

00:07:12.868 --> 00:07:14.601
-Well, don't listen to me
saying them out loud.

00:07:14.601 --> 00:07:17.234
-Well, you said it
at a normal volume.

00:07:17.234 --> 00:07:19.467
-We get to sniff it.

00:07:19.467 --> 00:07:21.801
-Am I going to get to answer
questions about the cracker?

00:07:21.801 --> 00:07:23.567
-The cracker is optional.

00:07:23.567 --> 00:07:25.267
It's to cleanse your palate.

00:07:25.267 --> 00:07:27.501
-How much do you like
or dislike the flavor?

00:07:27.501 --> 00:07:28.567
What was your answer?

00:07:28.567 --> 00:07:30.100
-I've got strong opinions,

00:07:30.100 --> 00:07:31.567
but the only one I'm sharing
with you out loud

00:07:31.567 --> 00:07:33.567
is the one about the cracker.

00:07:33.567 --> 00:07:35.567
I enjoyed it extremely.

00:07:35.567 --> 00:07:37.100
-How would you describe umami?

00:07:37.100 --> 00:07:38.634
-She's a sweet, Southern woman.

00:07:38.634 --> 00:07:39.801
[ Laughter ]

00:07:39.801 --> 00:07:42.634
-Not "you mommy." Umami.

00:07:42.634 --> 00:07:43.701
-Oh.

00:07:43.701 --> 00:07:45.234
[ Laughter ]
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:45.234 --> 00:07:48.267
-"Sweet, Southern woman."
Rhett &amp; Link, everybody.

00:07:48.267 --> 00:07:51.901
"Inside Eats with Rhett &amp; Link"
airs Sundays at 10:30 p.m.

00:07:51.901 --> 00:07:52.968
on Food Network.

